---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---
<Base
  title="My Approach to Therapy | Shloka Iyer, LMFT"
  description="Relational, psychodynamic and attachment-based therapy with a multicultural lens. Conversational online sessions for adults across California."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">My approach</p>
      <h1>A genuine therapeutic relationship, not a one-sided process</h1>
      <p class="lead">My style is conversational, engaged, and, at times, direct. I value authenticity in the therapy room and don't aim to be a blank slate.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white section--line">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">In the room</p>
        <h2>How I work</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <p>I strive to create a space where you feel comfortable bringing uncertainty, disagreement, humor, and the parts of yourself that don't often get expressed elsewhere.</p>
        <p>I approach therapy collaboratively rather than from a position of authority. This means clients are encouraged to question, reflect, and actively engage in the process.</p>
        <p>Some sessions are exploratory. Others are more structured. Together, we decide what feels most helpful based on what you're bringing into the room rather than following the same format every week.</p>
        <p>I tend to be direct when needed, and I also use humor where it feels appropriate. Therapy doesn't have to feel overly clinical to be meaningful, but it also doesn't become casual or unfocused.</p>
        <h3>Clients often describe my style as:</h3>
        <ul class="chips">
          <li>Direct</li>
          <li>Conversational</li>
          <li>Thoughtful</li>
          <li>Engaged</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--line">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Foundations</p>
        <h2>What informs my work</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <p>My work is primarily informed by relational, psychodynamic, attachment-based, existential, humanistic, and multicultural perspectives. Together, these approaches help us understand patterns, relationships, identity, and the meanings we make of our experiences.</p>
        <ul class="chips">
          <li>Psychodynamic therapy</li>
          <li>Relational approaches</li>
          <li>Attachment-based frameworks</li>
          <li>Existential and humanistic perspectives</li>
          <li>A multicultural, culturally responsive lens</li>
        </ul>
        <p>When helpful, I also incorporate elements of evidence-based approaches such as CBT and ACT. Rather than being the foundation of every session, these approaches are used selectively to introduce practical tools or different ways of approaching specific challenges.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white section--line">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">In session</p>
        <h2>What we might work on</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <p>Therapy is not about quickly fixing what feels difficult. Instead, our work may involve:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Understanding patterns that keep you feeling stuck or avoidant</li>
          <li>Developing language for emotions that have been hard to articulate</li>
          <li>Navigating relationships with more clarity and directness</li>
          <li>Examining expectations around identity, gender roles, and responsibility</li>
          <li>Making decisions that reflect who you are now</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Many clients begin therapy feeling disconnected or uncertain. Over time, they often become more comfortable examining their experiences rather than avoiding them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--line" id="how-therapy-works">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Process</p>
        <h2>How therapy works</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0">What to expect</h3>
        <p>Sessions are conversational. Some sessions are exploratory, while others focus on specific patterns or challenges.</p>
        <h3>Structure</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>No rigid worksheets or prescriptive exercises</li>
          <li>Occasional reflections between sessions</li>
          <li>Flexible structure based on your needs</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Therapy may include both exploration and gentle challenge, depending on what is most useful in the moment.</p>
        <h3>The process</h3>
        <p>Therapy is not about quick fixes. It is about understanding patterns, developing clarity, and building the ability to respond differently over time.</p>
        <h3>Who this may not suit</h3>
        <p>This approach may not be the best fit if you are looking for highly structured, worksheet-based therapy or a strictly directive style.</p>
        <p><a class="arrow-link" href="/guides/what-therapy-looks-like">Guide: what therapy looks like</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand heading="A consultation to determine fit" text="A 15-minute consultation is available to determine fit and answer any questions." />
</Base>
